 "docs": {
  "en": {
   "title": "Dog walks in Göteborg this weekend: no snow, but November rules give you room (14 November 2026)",
   "description": "Göteborg dog owners, weekend of 14 November 2026: 0 cm of snow measured around the city on Friday, a mild, mostly dry weekend. Where the leash rules are relaxed in November, the 12 fenced dog yards and Delsjöområdet.",
   "lede": "Göteborg has no snow for its dogs: the stations at Askim, Kållered and Härryda all measured 0 cm on Friday, and the weekend is mild, up to about 10 °C on Saturday. But November is a good month for dog walks here, because two of the city's seasonal leash rules are off.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "What the rules say in November",
     "p": [
      "The city asks for a lead in parks and plantings from 1 April to 30 September, and in nature from 1 March to 20 August. Both are outside those dates now. A dog off the lead must still be under control, and some places need a lead all year: market squares, bathing places, cemeteries, near schools and playgrounds, and Slottsskogen, except inside its fenced dog yard."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "The fenced dog yards",
     "p": [
      "Göteborg has 12 fenced hundrastgårdar, cleaned once a week. Among the largest are Keillers park, about 2000 m², and Hinsholmskilen, about 1750 m². Fjärdingsparken has 900 m². Slottsskogen's yard is near Majvallen in the western part of the park."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "A bigger walk: Delsjöområdet",
     "p": [
      "Delsjöområdet, on the eastern edge of the city, is a recreation area of about 1370 hectares of forest and lakes. In November the general rule for nature applies there: no seasonal leash requirement, but your dog must stay under control. Expect wet autumn paths rather than snow, and rain on Monday, roughly 9 to 16 mm."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "advice": [
    "Wet leaves and mud: a towel and a paw rinse at the door after Delsjön.",
    "Other walkers and joggers share the lake paths: call the dog in when people pass.",
    "For real snow with a dog this weekend, you would have to drive far north: the nearest white belt is in Dalarna."
   ],
   "captions": {
    "snow": "Snow depth measured at the weather stations on 13 November 2026: each dot is a station, coloured by its depth (light blue = a few cm, dark blue = deep); white dots with a grey ring = bare ground. Labels give the depth at the main stations. Measurements only, no model layer."
   },
   "method": "Snow depth today: measured at weather stations on the morning of 13 November 2026 (SMHI); a station reports the snow on its own small plot, so a few kilometres away and a hundred metres higher the ground can look different. Usual depth for the date: SnowScope snow history, 46 past winters (1980-81 to 2025-26), a model of the past at the city's height, not a station record. Weekend: two weather models (ECMWF IFS and DWD ICON, read through Open-Meteo), given as a range. Places and rules: the official pages listed below.",
   "references": [
    {
     "text": "SMHI, open meteorological observations (snow depth, daily)",
     "url": "https://www.smhi.se/data/meteorologi/ladda-ner-meteorologiska-observationer"
